To initialize a `RAJA::MultiReduceSum` object using a `std::vector` for initial values and retrieve the results back into the same vector, follow these steps:

1. Initialize your vector with the desired size and initial values.
2. Construct the `RAJA::MultiReduceSum` object using the vector.
3. Use the object in your kernel for reductions.
4. After kernel execution, call `get_all` to retrieve the results into the same vector.

Example:

```cpp
const int N = 1000;
const int B = 10;

// Initialize an array of length N and bin indices
int vec[N];
int bins[N];
for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {
  vec[i] = 1;
  bins[i] = i % B;
}

