Here’s the minimal Java implementation:

```java
class AsyncDatabaseRequest extends RichAsyncFunction<String, Tuple2<String, String>> {

    private transient DatabaseClient client;

    @Override
    public void open(OpenContext openContext) throws Exception {
        client = new DatabaseClient(host, port, credentials);
    }

    @Override
    public void asyncInvoke(String key, ResultFuture<Tuple2<String, String>> resultFuture) throws Exception {
        // Issue async request and handle result
        final Future<String> result = client.query(key);

        CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            try {
                return result.get();
            } catch (Exception e) {
                return null;
            }
        }).thenAccept(dbResult -> {
            resultFuture.complete(Collections.singleton(new Tuple2<>(key, dbResult)));
        });
    }
}
```

