To enable time travel queries for a table in Apache Flink, the `getTable(ObjectPath tablePath, long timestamp)` method must be implemented in a custom catalog. This method allows querying the historical state of a table at a specific timestamp.

Example implementation:

```java
public class MyCatalogSupportTimeTravel implements Catalog {

    @Override
    public CatalogBaseTable getTable(ObjectPath tablePath, long timestamp)
            throws TableNotExistException {
        Schema schema = buildSchema(timestamp);
        Map<String, String> options = buildOptions(timestamp);
        CatalogTable catalogTable =
                CatalogTable.newBuilder()
                        .schema(schema)
                        .comment("")
                        .partitionKeys(Collections.emptyList())
                        .options(options)
                        .snapshot(timestamp)
                        .build();
        return catalogTable;
    }
}
```

