To determine if two values are associated by comparing their insertion order in the maps, you compare the serial numbers (insertion order) of the values in their respective maps (`sn_mapL` and `sn_mapR`). If the serial numbers are equal, the values are considered associated. Otherwise, the one with the smaller serial number is considered less than the other.

Here's how it is done:

```c++
std::pair<iterator, bool> LeftRes = sn_mapL.insert(std::make_pair(Left, sn_mapL.size()));
std::pair<iterator, bool> RightRes = sn_mapR.insert(std::make_pair(Right, sn_mapR.size()));

if (LeftRes.first->second == RightRes.first->second)
    return 0;  // Values are associated
if (LeftRes.first->second < RightRes.first->second)
    return -1; // Left is considered less than Right
return 1;      // Right is considered less than Left
```

