To accumulate multiple `BadFileFormat` errors during an archive walk and handle them collectively after the walk completes, you can use the `joinErrors` utility to collect the errors into a `ErrorList`. After the walk, use `handleErrors` to manage them. Here's how it's done:

```cpp
Error walkArchive(Archive A) {
  Error DeferredErrs = Error::success();
  for (unsigned I = 0; I != A.numMembers(); ++I) {
    auto ChildOrErr = A.getMember(I);
    if (auto Err = ChildOrErr.takeError())
      if (Err.isA<BadFileFormat>())
        DeferredErrs = joinErrors(std::move(DeferredErrs), std::move(Err));
      else
        return Err;
    auto &Child = *ChildOrErr;
    // Use Child
    ...
  }
  return DeferredErrs;
}
```

Then, you can use `handleErrors(walkArchive(A))` to attempt to handle each of the collected `BadFileFormat` errors in sequence. If all are handled, it returns `Error::success()`; otherwise, it returns the unhandled errors in a `ErrorList`.

