Use the method shown in the `moveDbgRecordToStart` function. This function removes the specified `DbgVariableRecord` from its parent basic block, deletes all other debug records in the block for the same variable, and then reinserts the record at the beginning of the block.

Here is the relevant code:

```cpp
// New: Perform the same operation, but for a debug record.
void moveDbgRecordToStart(DbgVariableRecord *DVR) {
  BasicBlock *ParentBB = DVR->getParent();
  DVR->removeFromParent();
  for (Instruction &I : ParentBB) {
    for (auto &BlockDVR : filterDbgVars(I.getDbgRecordRange()))
      if (BlockDVR->getVariable() == DVR->getVariable())
